MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Enable kGlassFrame by default (macOS 26+; older systems keep the opaque
frame). Under glass, every Glint surface stops walling off the material:
the client-area backdrop (main_background_region — visible whenever a
side panel exists, i.e. always), the kNone top strip and toolbar (zero
opacity via upstream's ColorChoiceWithAlpha pattern; backgrounds must
exist — the layout CHECKs them), the side panel container and its themed
ContentParentBackground, and both color mixers' side panel pins (the
material mixer runs last and re-pins). The frame wash is dropped
entirely so panel, gutter and strip read as one bare glass surface.

Side panel web contents composite transparently: page base color +
WebContentsSetBackgroundColor helper, plus a live RWHV application in
OnLoaded — the helper only fires on future main-frame creation, and the
extension page commits in the initial frame (no process swap).

Toolbar icons go white over the dark glass (active/inactive/disabled,
pinned in both mixers).
